  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Consider the following set:\n\n$$\nA=\\{{Z}^{-},N,∅\\}\n$$\n\nGiven the relation $R$ on $A$ defined by\n\n$$\nX\\,R\\,Y\\,⇔\\,X\\cap Y⊃X,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${Z}^{-}R\\,N$\n\nII. $N\\,R\\,N$\n\nIII. ${Z}^{-}\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,∅$",
  "worked_solution": "A relation $R$ on a set $A$ is a subset of the Cartesian product $A\\times A={A}^{2}.$\n\n$$\nR⊆{A}^{2}\n$$\n\nWe also have the following notations:\n\n- $x\\,R\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\in R$\n\n- $x\\,\\cancel{\\,R\\,}\\,y$ if and only if $(x,y)\\notin R$\n\nIn this case, we have $X\\,R\\,Y$ if and only if $X\\cap Y⊃X.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. In this case, we have ${Z}^{-}\\cap N⊃{Z}^{-}.$ This is equivalent to ${Z}^{-}⊂{Z}^{-}\\cap N,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement II is false. In this case, we have $N\\cap N⊃N.$ This is equivalent to $N⊂N\\cap N,$ which is false.\n\n- Statement III is true. In this case, we have ${Z}^{-}\\cap ∅⊅{Z}^{-}.$ This is equivalent to ${Z}^{-}⊄{Z}^{-}\\cap ∅,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
